    "summary": "I built a three-storey tower on one cell. All three storeys use the North half base, because a drawer only fits on the cut face of a half base and the configurator only lets a half base stack on the same kind of half. The bottom storey has a classic drawer in its south cut face. The top storey holds a full-depth bin split into 3 compartments, with no cover on it so it stays open. The middle storey is just structure and is empty. I closed the open faces with end caps and bolted the joints. check_build found no rule errors and the collision check came back \"clear\". The build has 25 parts and prints as about 1454 g of filament.",
    "outcome": "built"
